# Line endings are part of this repository's contract, not a local preference.
#
# `backend/scripts/evidence_binding.py::contract_digests` takes a sha256 of the
# RAW BYTES of each file in `data/contract/`, and evidence files under
# `evidence/` record that digest as a permanent binding. Without the rules
# below, `core.autocrlf=true` (the Windows default, and set globally on at
# least one dev machine) rewrites those files to CRLF on checkout, so the
# digest pins the platform rather than the artifact.
#
# That is not hypothetical. Stories 1.9, 1.10 and 1.11 all recorded the CRLF
# digest of a Windows working copy — bytes that have never existed in the
# repository — and the divergence stayed invisible until the first Linux CI run
# computed the LF digest instead. `_dataset_file_digest` (evidence_binding.py)
# already documents the same hazard and worked around it by normalizing before
# hashing; these rules fix the cause instead, so a raw-byte digest finally means
# what its docstring says.
#
# `text eol=lf` rather than `-text` on the digest-bound paths on purpose:
# `-text` would stop git normalizing on COMMIT as well, letting an editor that
# writes CRLF put CRLF into the blob and move the digest again. `text eol=lf`
# pins LF in both directions.

# Default: normalize every detected text file to LF in the repository and check
# it out as LF everywhere, Windows included.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Digest-bound artifacts. Same rule as above, stated explicitly so it survives
# any future narrowing of the default and so the reason is greppable from here.
data/contract/**  text eol=lf
data/*.json       text eol=lf
evidence/**/*.json text eol=lf

# Shell scripts and CI config are executed by Linux runners; a CR would break
# the shebang line and produce `bad interpreter` / `unexpected token` errors.
*.sh                    text eol=lf
.github/**/*.yml        text eol=lf
.github/**/*.py         text eol=lf

# True binaries: never touch these bytes.
*.png   binary
*.jpg   binary
*.jpeg  binary
*.gif   binary
*.ico   binary
*.webp  binary
*.pdf   binary
*.zip   binary
*.db    binary
